  "prefLabel": "Ed 1118.01 Definitions",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ed 1118.01 Definitions. Except where the context makes another meaning clear, the following words have the meaning indicated when used in Ed 1118:\n\n(a) “Eligible offender with a disability” means an incarcerated person age 18 through 21 who:\n\n(1) Had been identified as a child with a disability prior to incarceration; and\n\n(2) Had an IEP prior to incarceration.\n\n(b) “State correctional facility” means the New Hampshire state prison for men or the New Hampshire state prison for women.\n\nSource. (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Ed 1100) #9197, eff 6-28-08; ss by #12141, eff 3-24-17",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ed1100.html"
